From 1a9dd5253bd6eec14b3ceab9e0b480c6da46b929 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:03:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RQ (VAX): default transfer time XTIME 1000 instructions (was
 200)

VMS V4.7 froze at boot, right after the date, when SYSINIT's 60 KB read
of F11BXQP.EXE completed within about 200 instructions of the poll:
SYSINIT then waits in RWAST for ever (known issues 97).  It happened
every time with SET NOASYNCH, and sometimes with asynchronous I/O when
the host was fully loaded (the I/O thread then completes within very few
simulated instructions).  Plain Open SIMH 87eb7d5 behaves the same.
XTIME 400 and more never froze; a real RQDX3/UDA50 takes milliseconds.
rq_io_complete() schedules a completion not before iostarttime + XTIME,
so the new default is also the minimum with asynchronous I/O.  The
PDP-11 version keeps 500.

Tested: microvax2 SET NOASYNCH 3 of 3 boots (before 0 of 3); two
simultaneous boots without IDLE 10 of 10 (before about half froze), with
SET NOASYNCH 6 of 6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SuavtcpUxEC2vXhit3JaAg
---
 PDP11/pdp11_rq.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/PDP11/pdp11_rq.c b/PDP11/pdp11_rq.c
index 2dc49e3e..446acbc2 100644
--- a/PDP11/pdp11_rq.c
+++ b/PDP11/pdp11_rq.c
@@ -154,7 +154,9 @@
 #elif defined (VM_VAX)                                  /* VAX version */
 #include "vax_defs.h"
 #define RQ_QTIME        100
-#define RQ_XTIME        200
+#define RQ_XTIME        1000                            /* VMS V4.7 boot misses a
+                                                           read that completes
+                                                           within ~200 instructions */
 #define OLDPC           fault_PC
 extern int32 fault_PC;
 
